{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792888316,"nonce":"z3k4iTR8ASkiPYi3H5vhvkdvJWA=","title":"The bytecode decoder spins forever on a file with no HashLink magic","message":"Passing a file that is not HashLink bytecode (a native Mach-O executable, in the RayDE report where `ash --build` hung) makes the header search loop at full CPU. The search keeps the last two bytes of each buffer in case the magic straddles a refill; once no more than two bytes are left it consumed nothing and looked again, so it never reached the end.\n\nFix: when two bytes or fewer remain, return the \"Could not find HashLink bytecode magic header\" error. Test: files of 0, 1, 2, 3, 100 and 70000 bytes that start with a Mach-O magic must all be refused.\n\nFound while looking at the RayDE AOT build that appeared stuck.","files":null}]}